#        - Tile i by a coarse factor (here, 256) to create an outer "tile"
#          loop and an inner loop over a tile.
#        - Further split the tile loop by a small factor (here, 4) and fully
#          unroll that innermost loop. This yields a partial unroll of 4
#          iterations while keeping code size reasonable.
#        - Parallelize the outer tile loops with OpenMP. Each tile operates
#          on a disjoint subset of indices, so this is safe.
#
#   2. Finally, rename the scheduled procedure to 'kernel_jacobi_1d'
#      so the generated C function matches the driver’s expectation.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

